8. FTLE — Fault Tolerant Learn Edition

FTLE provides the continuous-learning and reassessment component.

Its central function is to prevent previous errors, incomplete information, and outdated assumptions from becoming permanent institutional conclusions.

FTLE operating controls

1. Detect new evidence.
2. Compare new information with previous findings.
3. Identify contradictions.
4. Reopen affected research classifications.
5. Reassess applicable legal authority.
6. Record corrective changes.
7. Preserve previous versions.
8. Publish updated research status.

FTLE principle: An institutional conclusion must remain revisable when materially relevant evidence changes.


